  "solution": {
    "text": "The electronic configuration can be written as,<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mn>6</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>3</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>3</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mn>6</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>4</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>3</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mn>10</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>4</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mn>6</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>5</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></math><br /><br />The outermost electron has i.e.,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mmultiscripts><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mi>Kr</mi></mfenced><mprescripts></mprescripts><mn>36</mn><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts><mn>5</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></math><br /><br />Principal quantum number<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></math><br /><br />Azimuthal quantum number<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> (corresponds to s)<br /><br />Magnetic quantum number<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math><br /><br />Spin quantum number<math> <mrow> <mo>=</mo> <mo>+</mo> <mfrac> <mrow> <mn>1</mn> </mrow> <mrow> <mn>2</mn> </mrow> </mfrac> </mrow> </math> (positive spin)"
  }
